 ## Overview
-The OpenGL GPU Multi Volume Ray Cast Mapper is an OpenGL-specific subclass of the GPU Multi-Volume Ray Casting Mapper that handles hardware extension checks, OpenGL object lifecycle management, and clipping/cropping plane setup for GPU-accelerated volume rendering [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the concrete implementation responsible for drawing the volume ray cast image to the screen by managing the fragment shader programs, framebuffer objects, and texture uploads required for rendering multiple volumes simultaneously [S2, unofficial]. It builds on [GPU Multi-Volume Ray Casting Mapper](2461-gpu-multi-volume-ray-casting-mapper.md) by providing the specific OpenGL API bindings and state management necessary for hardware-accelerated ray casting.
